From: Unlatch <noreply@github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntfs_boot_sector_parse: reject sector counts that overflow

number_of_sectors comes from the boot sector unchecked, and
"(sectors - 1) << sector_size_bits" is undefined behaviour (signed
overflow) for large or negative values. Reject them before the shift.

Found by Unlatch's libFuzzer target fuzz_probe with UBSan (Step 07).
---
--- a/libntfs-3g/bootsect.c	2026-11-01 13:59:55
+++ b/libntfs-3g/bootsect.c	2026-11-01 13:59:55
@@ -223,6 +223,16 @@
 	ntfs_log_debug("NumberOfSectors = %lld\n", (long long)sectors);
 	if (!sectors) {
 		ntfs_log_error("Volume size is set to zero.\n");
+		return -1;
+	}
+	/*
+	 * Reject sizes whose byte offset cannot be represented, so the
+	 * shift below cannot overflow (Unlatch patch 0002, found by fuzzing).
+	 */
+	if ((sectors < 0)
+	    || ((sectors - 1) > ((s64)(~(u64)0 >> 1) >> vol->sector_size_bits))) {
+		ntfs_log_error("Volume size %lld sectors is invalid.\n",
+			       (long long)sectors);
 		return -1;
 	}
